-- dispatch: the `field` target (§7.1, §8.3). A receiver whose type is known
-- at the call and turns out to be a RECORD is a field call — `language.md`
-- §6.3 unchanged — so `handler.run 1` means `(handler.run) 1` and the table
-- says `field`. That is the row S4 must keep lowering the way it does
-- today, and it is the difference between §1.2's resolution table and
-- §6.3's discharge table: a constraint that was DEFERRED and only later met
-- a record is `no_methods_on_shape` instead (§11's deferred-receiver row,
-- `check/bad/MethodOnTuple` and the hint in §10.3).
pub type alias Handler =
    { name : String, run : Int -> Int }


pub invoke : Handler -> Int
invoke handler =
    handler.run 1
